  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "**TX-0401 amount verified:** EUR 240.00, outgoing card payment to TechMart Online on 2026-07-20, status settled. The account is ACC-1005 (EUR, balance EUR 1,310.20).\n\nI also noticed TX-0402: EUR 240.00 to the same merchant on 2026-07-14, also settled. I'm pointing it out only as a fact from your records.\n\n**Reason codes that could apply to a settled card payment:**\n\n- **duplicate_charge**: the same purchase was charged more than once. TX-0401 and TX-0402 match in amount and merchant, so this is worth considering if you were billed once for one purchase.\n- **unauthorized_debit**: you did not authorise the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present**: an online card payment was made using your card details without your involvement.\n- **goods_not_received**: you paid for something and did not receive it.\n- **service_not_rendered**: you paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nWhich of these fits depends on what happened. Tell me, and I will check eligibility for the matching code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute without your confirmation.",
